  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Security and Livelihoods in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NPA&apos;s Food security and livelihoods (FSL) programme in Lebanon responds to the needs of vulnerable Lebanese and Palestinian host communities and refugee families from Syria and strengthens community resilience, including analysis based on gender, age and disability. The communities are provided with food assistance in the form of either food parcels or ready-to-consume meals, as well as offered Cash for Work (CfW) assistance in the fields of construction, agriculture, and environmental services. NPA fosters environmental sustainability and community sustenance through a multi-faceted support that includes trainings and provisions of equipment to farmers.</narrative>
  </description>
